<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Evaluating permutations using the nPr factorial formula</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Complete the working step by step to evaluate each permutation. Recall the permutation formula:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_nP_r = \frac{n!}{(n - r)!}\)</p>

<p><b>Part A: A bus has \({@n1@}\) passengers waiting at a stage and \(3\) empty seats. Find \({}_{{@n1@}}P_{3}\), the number of ways to seat \(3\) of the passengers.</b></p>
<ol>
  <li>Substitute \(n = {@n1@}\) and \(r = 3\) into the permutation formula:<br>
  \(\displaystyle {}_{{@n1@}}P_{3} = \frac{{@n1@}!}{({@n1@} - 3)!} =\)
  <span style="display:inline-flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; vertical-align:middle; margin:0 4px;">
    <span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000; padding:0 6px;">\({@n1@}!\)</span>
    <span style="padding-top:3px;">[[input:ans1]]</span>
  </span>
  [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]
  </li>
  <li>Expand \({@n1@}!\) in the numerator only as far as \({@k1@}!\), then cancel the common factor:<br>
  \(\displaystyle \frac{{@n1@}!}{{@k1@}!} = \frac{{@n1@} \times {@m1_1@} \times {@m1_2@} \times {@k1@}!}{{@k1@}!} = {@n1@} \times {@m1_1@} \times\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]
  </li>
  <li>Multiply the remaining \(3\) descending factors to find \({}_{{@n1@}}P_{3}\):<br>
  \(\displaystyle {}_{{@n1@}}P_{3} = {@n1@} \times {@m1_1@} \times {@m1_2@} =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]
  </li>
</ol>

<p><b>Part B: A school elects a Prefect and an Assistant Prefect (\(2\) distinct positions) from \({@n2@}\) candidates. Find \({}_{{@n2@}}P_{2}\).</b></p>
<ol>
  <li>Substitute \(n = {@n2@}\) and \(r = 2\) into the permutation formula:<br>
  \(\displaystyle {}_{{@n2@}}P_{2} = \frac{{@n2@}!}{({@n2@} - 2)!} =\)
  <span style="display:inline-flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; vertical-align:middle; margin:0 4px;">
    <span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000; padding:0 6px;">\({@n2@}!\)</span>
    <span style="padding-top:3px;">[[input:ans4]]</span>
  </span>
  [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]
  </li>
  <li>Expand \({@n2@}!\) in the numerator only as far as \({@k2@}!\), then cancel the common factor:<br>
  \(\displaystyle \frac{{@n2@}!}{{@k2@}!} = \frac{{@n2@} \times {@m2_1@} \times {@k2@}!}{{@k2@}!} = {@n2@} \times\) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]
  </li>
  <li>Multiply the remaining \(2\) descending factors to find \({}_{{@n2@}}P_{2}\):<br>
  \(\displaystyle {}_{{@n2@}}P_{2} = {@n2@} \times {@m2_1@} =\) [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt6]]
  </li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>The permutation formula \(\displaystyle {}_nP_r = \frac{n!}{(n - r)!}\) simplifies to the product of \(r\) consecutive descending integers starting at \(n\).</p>

<p><b>Part A: Evaluating \({}_{{@n1@}}P_{3}\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{{@n1@}}P_{3} = \frac{{@n1@}!}{({@n1@} - 3)!} = \frac{{@n1@}!}{{@k1@}!}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">Expand \({@n1@}!\) until it matches \({@k1@}!\) and cancel the common factor:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle = \frac{{@n1@} \times {@m1_1@} \times {@m1_2@} \times {@k1@}!}{{@k1@}!} = {@n1@} \times {@m1_1@} \times {@m1_2@} = {@ta3@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {}_{{@n1@}}P_{3} = {@ta3@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part B: Evaluating \({}_{{@n2@}}P_{2}\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{{@n2@}}P_{2} = \frac{{@n2@}!}{({@n2@} - 2)!} = \frac{{@n2@}!}{{@k2@}!}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">Expand \({@n2@}!\) until it matches \({@k2@}!\) and cancel the common factor:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle = \frac{{@n2@} \times {@m2_1@} \times {@k2@}!}{{@k2@}!} = {@n2@} \times {@m2_1@} = {@ta6@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {}_{{@n2@}}P_{2} = {@ta6@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
